  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Conceptualizing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interface. The goal is a web application with a Windows desktop aesthetic. I\'m exploring layouts that achieve a professional, clean, and structured feel. I want it to be intuitive and visually appealing, while mimicking the familiar Windows design paradigm.\n\n\n**Defining Cost Components**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the specifics of quarry cost accounting. I\'ve broken down the calculation into key production processes: extraction, transport, crushing, loading, and general overhead. For each stage, I\'m identifying the necessary elements, including internal equipment costs, external equipment rentals, personnel expenses (salaries, meals, lodging), and various taxes.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Requirements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI specifications, emphasizing a Windows-style desktop application look and feel. The app *must* be in French, be fully responsive, and function optimally on a desktop. I\'m prioritizing features such as local storage for saving simulations, multiple scenario creation, and report generation (PDF, CSV/Excel), as well as interactive breakdown charts (pie, bar, cost/ton). I\'m also checking skills to see if any are relevant.\n\n\n**Clarifying Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m now solidifying the application\'s architecture as a clean React client-side application. The goal is a rich dashboard with interactive charts, a clear cost structure, scenario simulation capabilities, and export options. Visual appeal is key, aiming for a \"Windows ERP/Dashboard\" or modern slate design. No need for Firebase or other external databases, per the user\'s requirements.\n\n\n"
