  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Layout**\n\nI\'ve successfully installed `recharts`, a great start. My focus has now shifted to designing the application\'s layout. I\'m starting to visualize the core components and their types, keeping in mind the user\'s request for a clear representation of the quarry\'s five key processes.\n\n\n**Defining the Data Structure**\n\nNow I\'m diving deep into the data requirements for each of the quarry\'s processes. I\'m breaking down \"Forage, Blasting/Minage, Extraction\" and the subsequent processes into their constituent cost elements. Specifically, I am focusing on the user\'s need to capture detailed information on both internal and external equipment costs, as well as personnel expenses and relevant taxes. I\'m structuring data fields for fuel consumption, spare parts, equipment depreciation, rental costs, salaries, meals, accommodation, and taxes related to each of the five processes.\n\n\n**Incorporating Production Metrics**\n\nI\'ve added the crucial overall production metrics, specifically the total production volume and the target cost price calculation. The user\'s focus on the cost per tonne is now central to the structure. I\'m also preparing to organize the codebase. I intend to create clear data types, default templates for realistic quarry scenarios (with selectable currencies, defaulting to Euro or Custom), and a well-structured component directory.\n\n\n**Planning the Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on the user interface components. I\'ve broken down the application into key sections: a header control bar, process input sections, a dashboard for summary views, a scenario manager for data handling, and an equipment catalog. My immediate focus is on designing the process input interface, aiming for a granular approach that allows detailed input for each machine within a process, alongside a quick-entry mode. The intention is to cater to both detailed cost breakdowns and streamlined data entry.\n\n\n**Detailing Equipment Costs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on equipment cost specifics. I\'ve broken down equipment input, including detailed fields like name, work hours, fuel consumption, spare parts and maintenance, and depreciation. I\'m also including a quick-entry option for global values. For external/rented equipment, I am adding fields for name, rental duration, and rate. Finally, personnel expense input is being considered.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `/src/types.ts` file to define the structured data model for our quarry cost accounting software. This includes types for internal equipment, rented machinery, personnel expenses, taxes, and production processes. This will ensure full type-safety and support advanced calculations (fuel consumption, depreciation, and lodging)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 546932793
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
