  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Calculation Helpers**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating utility functions for detailed cost calculations and scenario summarization. I\'m putting these helper functions into `/src/utils/calculations.ts` to keep the code modular and well-organized. I am moving on to designing the calculations, starting with the `MachineInterne` type.\n\n\n**Defining Cost Formulas**\n\nI\'ve defined formulas for Gasoil, Spare Parts, and Depreciation costs. If direct entry (`isSaisieDirecte`) is true, I\'m using the global values. Otherwise, calculations are done based on usage, consumption, and amortization. I also considered proration based on the scenario type. Finally, I\'ve outlined calculations for both `MachineExterne` and `PersonnelCharges`, including handling of base salaries with and without direct input.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a helper calculation utility `/src/utils/calculations.ts` to calculate costs dynamically for all elements (internal equipment, rental equipment, personnel salaries/meals/lodging, and production-based taxes) prorated properly by the selected period (mensuel or annuel). This will keep the math clean and centralized."
