  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Tailwind Configuration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed Tailwind v4 is correctly set up in `src/index.css`. Currently, I\'m analyzing the font imports \342\200\223 `Inter` and `JetBrains Mono` are the present focus. Digging into the \"Bold Typography\" theme, `font-sans` with `font-black` (weight 900) or other heavy weights are noted.\n\n\n**Analyzing Design Parameters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific design parameters. I\'m noting the use of `tracking-tighter` for titles and the high-contrast color scheme, including deep zinc backgrounds, dark gray blocks, and emerald text. I\'m reviewing requested HTML to extract layout patterns and element styles, such as for the app container, top header, and active states with specific classes. I\'m focusing on exact styling and classes, like `QUARRY_CORE.v1` styling.\n\n\n**Adapting Themes to React**\n\nI\'m getting this elegant style translated for the React app. I\'ve noted examples like `bg-zinc-100 text-black p-5 flex flex-col`. I\'m going to alter the root layout in `App.tsx`: changing `bg-slate-50` to `bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100`. I\'m working on header styles and sidebar adaptations to complete the theme transformation.\n\n\n**Implementing Button Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now implementing the button styling. My focus is on matching the active and inactive states precisely. I\'ve noted the brutalist theme with its emerald and zinc colors, and the `uppercase` and `font-black` classes. I will apply these classes, including the requested `rounded-none`, to sidebar navigation buttons. I\'m aiming to keep functionality while applying the requested visual changes.\n\n\n**Refining Style Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating active/inactive button styles: using emerald for active, zinc for inactive, both with uppercase, bold font, and no rounding. I am also adjusting the settings panel block, and ensuring inputs have the specified zinc background, borders, and text colors. I\'ve switched input and select elements to use font-mono. I am also planning to apply this styling to the Dashboard KPI cards.\n\n\n**Defining Color Classes**\n\nI\'m now defining color classes. I\'ve established the classes for highlighting with top borders: `primary`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`, and `info`. I also defined `neutral` with a light background and black text, taking inspiration from the personnel block in the design, and an edge border. I\'m noting the title text classes (`text-xs font-black text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-widest`), and value text classes (`text-4xl font-black italic tracking-tight`).\n\n\n**Styling Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating subvalue text with `mt-2 text-[10px] font-bold text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider`. The plan is to style the icon wrapper with either `p-2 rounded-none bg-zinc-950 text-white` or `bg-zinc-200 text-black` depending on the light or dark card context. I\'ve begun styling dashboard tables to be very clean, technical, and brutalist. I\'m focusing on defining header, row, and input styles for that section, as well as applying highlighting to total rows with emerald tones. I intend to adjust Recharts elements with similar color schemes.\n\n\n**Styling Visualizations Details**\n\nI am now focusing on chart visualizations for dark mode. I\'ve chosen vibrant colors like Emerald and White. The wrapper is now `bg-zinc-900 border-2 border-zinc-800 text-white rounded-none`. I\'m also adjusting the tooltip to have dark mode styles: background `#18181b`, text white, and a border. I am applying styles to the Process Editor view, and am working on styling table headers.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 861837062
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
