    thinking: "**Prioritizing Design Compliance**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on ensuring the design rules are fully respected. Currently, I\'m prioritizing the layout and elements, as well as the bold typography design theme. I\'ve decided to modify `src/index.css` initially to set the standard colors, layout borders, and typographic properties. I am now double checking before moving forward.\n\n\n**Refining The Style**\n\nI\'m now diving into the details within `src/index.css`. I\'m starting to define utility styles for a \"pure, gorgeous brutalist\" look, which is exciting! I\'m overriding the body element with dark background and light text, using `bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100 font-sans` in `@layer base`. A major breakthrough: I\'ve come up with a way to make `.rounded-xl` elements look brutalist in a dark theme by overriding their properties in CSS! This will allow automatic application of a brutalist theme without manual class changes in React components.\n\n\n**Mapping Color Themes**\n\nOkay, I\'m analyzing the existing class names to map to a dark theme. I\'ve identified the main culprits: `.bg-white`, `.bg-slate-50`, and text classes. I\'m thinking of mapping `.bg-white` to a dark background. Next, I\'ll figure out what color values will best provide visual contrast for the typography, while maintaining the elegance I am looking for. I am also planning on overriding those rounded corners!\n\n\n**Implementing Flat Corners**\n\nI\'m now focusing on removing rounded corners under the dark theme, and I\'ve identified key elements: grid blocks, the personnel section, and the footer. I\'ve decided to override these corner styles in `src/index.css` using `border-radius: 0px !important;`. The goal is to fully embrace a \"flat corners\" brutalist theme. I\'m moving on to defining typography styles: display titles should use `font-black tracking-tighter uppercase`. I plan to define styles for `#app-root` in `src/index.css` to transform the components.\n\n\n**Adjusting Uppercase Headers**\n\nOkay, I\'m reconsidering the uppercase approach. Initially, I thought that uppercase headers would be perfect, but now I think I should be more flexible. I\'m focusing on applying `font-black tracking-tighter` more widely for a bold look, which I feel will improve the visual quality. This will apply a punch, and I\'ll consider custom utility classes. Finally, I\'m checking the specific color values to ensure a premium, polished design. I\'m excited with the direction I\'m taking!\n\n\n**Defining Color Accents**\n\nI\'m now integrating color accents for statuses, using emerald-500, amber-500, and red-500. I am re-examining `src/index.css` to add the new styles. Further, I\'m focusing on making cards flat and adjusting backgrounds and text colors inside `#app-root`. I plan on replacing blue accents with emerald green for visual consistency. Finally, I\'m going to check `src/App.js` to ensure coherent application of the brutalist theme.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 475788932
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
