    thinking: "**Verifying template integrity**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve just updated the default template; it\'s got explosives in the taille\'s front and external rentals across the processes. Now, I need to check `alternativeTemplates` to make sure there are no empty models or other problematic templates in the mix. I\'m keen to make sure this is solid.\n\n\n**Migrating Saved Scenarios**\n\nOkay, I\'ve dug into potential issues with saved user scenarios. It seems that if someone has an older scenario loaded in their browser, it might be missing the explosives or external rentals added in the new default scenario. To address this, I\'m thinking of creating a \"migration\" function in `App.tsx` or `calculations/templates`. This will automatically upgrade any loaded scenario to include the missing elements: the explosives in the `front_de_taille` and the external machines for each process. I think this will maintain data integrity.\n\n\n**Implementing scenario upgrade**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a clearer picture now. I\'m going to introduce the upgrade within `src/App.tsx`, specifically when a scenario loads. I\'ll need a helper function, `ensureRequiredItems`, that checks for the explosives in the `front_de_taille` and the external rentals. It will add them if they are missing. This feels like the cleanest and most reliable way to handle the migration.\n\n\n**Refining item insertion**\n\nI\'m now honing the `ensureRequiredItems` helper. It ensures that \'me-ft-explosifs\' is present within `de_taille.machinesExternes`. Furthermore, I\'ve got to check and ensure that locations like \'me-ft-location\', \'me-co-loc\', and \'me-ch-loc\' exist in their respective processes, adding them if they\'re absent. This approach guarantees immediate inclusion of these crucial items upon loading a saved scenario. I plan to put this in `src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adding specific locations**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of adding external machines within `ensureRequiredItems`. I\'m focusing on ensuring specific locations are present in each process. I\'m adding `me-ft-location` to `front_de_taille`, a dumper `me-tr-1` for transport, and `me-co-loc` for concassage, among others. These are crucial for ensuring the scenarios are comprehensive and correct after an upgrade.\n\n\n"
